direct relationship between the nature and quality of the product required and the payment made
by the customer. Therefore, the Concrete Construction Worker has a continuing responsibility to
work professionally in order to meet the requirements of the customer and thus maintain and grow
the business.', 510, 510, '401–600', 'Version', '06 Feb 2024', '06 Feb 2026', 'Construction Skill Development Council of India (CSDCI)', 'Construction Skill Development Council of India', 'Skill Competitions', 'N/A', 'General Qualification', 'N.A.', '{"Theory":"150","Practical":"360","EmployabilitySkills":"00","OJT_Mandatory":"00"}', false, '{}'::text[], '{"source_row": "34", "qualification_type": "General Qualification", "version": "Version"}'::jsonb, 'Qualifications 02-10-2026 20_02_11.xlsx', true) ON CONFLICT (q_code, title) DO UPDATE SET sector_id = EXCLUDED.sector_id, nsqf_level = EXCLUDED.nsqf_level, description = EXCLUDED.description, min_notional_hours = EXCLUDED.min_notional_hours, max_notional_hours = EXCLUDED.max_notional_hours, notional_hours_range = EXCLUDED.notional_hours_range, is_pwd = EXCLUDED.is_pwd, pwd_categories = EXCLUDED.pwd_categories, updated_at = NOW();
INSERT INTO nsqf_qualifications (q_code, title, sector_id, sector_name, nsqf_level, description, min_notional_hours, max_notional_hours, notional_hours_range, version, originally_approved, valid_till, awarding_body, certifying_bodies, proposed_occupation, progression_pathway, qualification_type, adopted_qualification, training_delivery_hours, is_pwd, pwd_categories, raw_metadata, source_file, is_active) VALUES ('QG-4.5-CO-01794-2024-V1-CSDCI, v 1.0', 'Digital Construction (WorldSkills)', 'construction', 'Construction', 4.5, 'Digital Construction using Building Information Modelling (BIM) is a process for creating and
managing information on a construction project across the project lifecycle. One of the key outputs
of this process is the digital Building Information Model, the digital description of every aspect of the
built asset. This digital model draws on information assembled collaboratively and updated at key
stages of a project. Creating a digital Building Information Model enables those who interact with
the building to optimise their actions, resulting in a more excellent whole life value for the asset.', 510, 510, '401–600', 'Version', '06 Feb 2024', '06 Feb 2026', 'Construction Skill Development Council of India (CSDCI)', 'Construction Skill Development Council of India', 'Skill Competitions', 'N/A', 'General Qualification', 'N.A.', '{"Theory":"150","Practical":"360","EmployabilitySkills":"00","OJT_Mandatory":"00"}', false, '{}'::text[], '{"source_row": "35", "qualification_type": "General Qualification", "version": "Version"}'::jsonb, 'Qualifications 02-10-2026 20_02_11.xlsx', true) ON CONFLICT (q_code, title) DO UPDATE SET sector_id = EXCLUDED.sector_id, nsqf_level = EXCLUDED.nsqf_level, description = EXCLUDED.description, min_notional_hours = EXCLUDED.min_notional_hours, max_notional_hours = EXCLUDED.max_notional_hours, notional_hours_range = EXCLUDED.notional_hours_range, is_pwd = EXCLUDED.is_pwd, pwd_categories = EXCLUDED.pwd_categories, updated_at = NOW();
INSERT INTO nsqf_qualifications (q_code, title, sector_id, sector_name, nsqf_level, description, min_notional_hours, max_notional_hours, notional_hours_range, version, originally_approved, valid_till, awarding_body, certifying_bodies, proposed_occupation, progression_pathway, qualification_type, adopted_qualification, training_delivery_hours, is_pwd, pwd_categories, raw_metadata, source_file, is_active) VALUES ('QG-4.5-CO-01788-2024-V1-CSDCI', 'Painting and Decorating (WorldSkills)', 'construction', 'Construction', 4.5, 'A painter and decorator works in the commercial and public sectors and is responsible for the
external and internal appearance of a building and its protection from water, rust, corrosion, mould,
and insect infestation. There is a direct relationship between the nature and quality of the service
required and the payment made by the client. Therefore, the painter and decorator has a
continuing responsibility to work professionally and interactively with the client in order to give
satisfaction and thus maintain and grow the business.', 510, 510, '401–600', 'Version', '06 Feb 2024', '06 Feb 2026', 'Construction Skill Development Council of India (CSDCI)', 'Construction Skill Development Council of India', 'Construction Painting', 'N/A', 'General Qualification', 'N.A.', '{"Theory":"150","Practical":"360","EmployabilitySkills":"00","OJT_Mandatory":"00"}', false, '{}'::text[], '{"source_row": "36", "qualification_type": "General Qualification", "version": "Version"}'::jsonb, 'Qualifications 02-10-2026 20_02_11.xlsx', true) ON CONFLICT (q_code, title) DO UPDATE SET sector_id = EXCLUDED.sector_id, nsqf_level = EXCLUDED.nsqf_level, description = EXCLUDED.description, min_notional_hours = EXCLUDED.min_notional_hours, max_notional_hours = EXCLUDED.max_notional_hours, notional_hours_range = EXCLUDED.notional_hours_range, is_pwd = EXCLUDED.is_pwd, pwd_categories = EXCLUDED.pwd_categories, updated_at = NOW();
INSERT INTO nsqf_qualifications (q_code, title, sector_id, sector_name, nsqf_level, description, min_notional_hours, max_notional_hours, notional_hours_range, version, originally_approved, valid_till, awarding_body, certifying_bodies, proposed_occupation, progression_pathway, qualification_type, adopted_qualification, training_delivery_hours, is_pwd, pwd_categories, raw_metadata, source_file, is_active) VALUES ('QG-4.5-CO-01787-2024-V1-CSDCI', 'Plastering and Drywall Systems (WorldSkills)', 'construction', 'Construction', 4.5, 'The skilled plasterer may work on both internal and external plastering and rendering work. Much
modern internal work is completed using drywall systems which involve the plasterer creating metal
frames and installing plasterboard before the application on the final surface. These constructions
can be complex and include curves and openings for doors and windows. Traditional plastering
involves the preparation of the background prior to application of the plaster surface. The plasterer
will prepare materials for use and be fully aware of legislation and official guidance relating to the
preparation and use of materials. In addition to plastering flat surfaces, the skilled plasterer will
create and install decorative mouldings. Plasterers will also be required to make repairs.', 510, 510, '401–600', 'Version', '06 Feb 2024', '06 Feb 2026', 'Construction Skill Development Council of India (CSDCI)', 'Construction Skill Development Council of India', 'For Skill Competitions', 'N/A', 'Upskilling Qualification', 'N.A.', '{"Theory":"150","Practical":"360","EmployabilitySkills":"00","OJT_Mandatory":"00"}', false, '{}'::text[], '{"source_row": "37", "qualification_type": "Upskilling Qualification", "version": "Version"}'::jsonb, 'Qualifications 02-10-2026 20_02_11.xlsx', true) ON CONFLICT (q_code, title) DO UPDATE SET sector_id = EXCLUDED.sector_id, nsqf_level = EXCLUDED.nsqf_level, description = EXCLUDED.description, min_notional_hours = EXCLUDED.min_notional_hours, max_notional_hours = EXCLUDED.max_notional_hours, notional_hours_range = EXCLUDED.notional_hours_range, is_pwd = EXCLUDED.is_pwd, pwd_categories = EXCLUDED.pwd_categories, updated_at = NOW();
INSERT INTO nsqf_qualifications (q_code, title, sector_id, sector_name, nsqf_level, description, min_notional_hours, max_notional_hours, notional_hours_range, version, originally_approved, valid_till, awarding_body, certifying_bodies, proposed_occupation, progression_pathway, qualification_type, adopted_qualification, training_delivery_hours, is_pwd, pwd_categories, raw_metadata, source_file, is_active) VALUES ('QG-4.5-CO-01783-2024-V1-CSDCI', 'Wall and Floor Tiling (WorldSkills)', 'construction', 'Construction', 4.5, 'A tiler generally works on commercial and residential projects. There is a direct relationship
between the nature and quality of the product required and the payment made by the customer.
Therefore, the tiler has a continuing responsibility to work professionally in order to meet the
requirements of the customer and thus maintain and grow the business. Tiling is closely associated
with other parts of the construction industry, and with the many products that support it, normally for
commercial purposes.', 510, 510, '401–600', 'Version', '06 Feb 2024', '06 Feb 2026', 'Construction Skill Development Council of India (CSDCI)', 'Construction Skill Development Council of India', 'Skill Competitions', 'N/A', 'General Qualification', 'N.A.', '{"Theory":"150","Practical":"360","EmployabilitySkills":"00","OJT_Mandatory":"00"}', false, '{}'::text[], '{"source_row": "38", "qualification_type": "General Qualification", "version": "Version"}'::jsonb, 'Qualifications 02-10-2026 20_02_11.xlsx', true) ON CONFLICT (q_code, title) DO UPDATE SET sector_id = EXCLUDED.sector_id, nsqf_level = EXCLUDED.nsqf_level, description = EXCLUDED.description, min_notional_hours = EXCLUDED.min_notional_hours, max_notional_hours = EXCLUDED.max_notional_hours, notional_hours_range = EXCLUDED.notional_hours_range, is_pwd = EXCLUDED.is_pwd, pwd_categories = EXCLUDED.pwd_categories, updated_at = NOW();
INSERT INTO nsqf_qualifications (q_code, title, sector_id, sector_name, nsqf_level, description, min_notional_hours, max_notional_hours, notional_hours_range, version, originally_approved, valid_till, awarding_body, certifying_bodies, proposed_occupation, progression_pathway, qualification_type, adopted_qualification, training_delivery_hours, is_pwd, pwd_categories, raw_metadata, source_file, is_active) VALUES ('NG-03-CO-02343-2024-V1-CSDCI', 'Brick Mason (Advance)', 'construction', 'Construction', 3.0, 'A Brick Mason – Advanced is an experienced professional who is responsible for constructing and repairing structures, such as walls, partitions, facades and other masonry structures using bricks, stones, concrete blocks and other building blocks and masonry materials. The individual uses different types of brick masonry tools and equipment, including basic and advanced. The person acts as a small entrepreneur, setting up and managing a brick masonry enterprise.', 120, 120, '1–200', 'Version', '15 Mar 2024', '15 Mar 2027', 'Construction Skill Development Council of India (CSDCI)', 'Construction Skill Development Council of India', 'N/A', 'N/A', 'General Qualification', 'N.A.', '{"Theory":"120","Practical":"00","EmployabilitySkills":"00","OJT_Mandatory":"00"}', false, '{}'::text[], '{"source_row": "39", "qualification_type": "General Qualification", "version": "Version"}'::jsonb, 'Qualifications 02-10-2026 20_02_11.xlsx', true) ON CONFLICT (q_code, title) DO UPDATE SET sector_id = EXCLUDED.sector_id, nsqf_level = EXCLUDED.nsqf_level, description = EXCLUDED.description, min_notional_hours = EXCLUDED.min_notional_hours, max_notional_hours = EXCLUDED.max_notional_hours, notional_hours_range = EXCLUDED.notional_hours_range, is_pwd = EXCLUDED.is_pwd, pwd_categories = EXCLUDED.pwd_categories, updated_at = NOW();
INSERT INTO nsqf_qualifications (q_code, title, sector_id, sector_name, nsqf_level, description, min_notional_hours, max_notional_hours, notional_hours_range, version, originally_approved, valid_till, awarding_body, certifying_bodies, proposed_occupation, progression_pathway, qualification_type, adopted_qualification, training_delivery_hours, is_pwd, pwd_categories, raw_metadata, source_file, is_active) VALUES ('NG-03-CO-02344-2024-V1-CSDCI', 'Concrete Mason - Advanced', 'construction', 'Construction', 3.0, 'A Concrete Mason - Advanced is responsible for leading and executing various concrete construction projects, overseeing a team of masons and ensuring the successful completion of projects within specified timelines and quality standards. He will utilize advanced techniques and methods to work with concrete, including forming, pouring, finishing and repairing structures such as foundations, walls, floors and sidewalks.', 120, 120, '1–200', 'Version', '15 Mar 2024', '15 Mar 2027', 'Construction Skill Development Council of India (CSDCI)', 'Construction Skill Development Council of India', 'N/A', 'N/A', 'General Qualification', 'N.A.', '{"Theory":"120","Practical":"00","EmployabilitySkills":"00","OJT_Mandatory":"00"}', false, '{}'::text[], '{"source_row": "40", "qualification_type": "General Qualification", "version": "Version"}'::jsonb, 'Qualifications 02-10-2026 20_02_11.xlsx', true) ON CONFLICT (q_code, title) DO UPDATE SET sector_id = EXCLUDED.sector_id, nsqf_level = EXCLUDED.nsqf_level, description = EXCLUDED.description, min_notional_hours = EXCLUDED.min_notional_hours, max_notional_hours = EXCLUDED.max_notional_hours, notional_hours_range = EXCLUDED.notional_hours_range, is_pwd = EXCLUDED.is_pwd, pwd_categories = EXCLUDED.pwd_categories, updated_at = NOW();
INSERT INTO nsqf_qualifications (q_code, title, sector_id, sector_name, nsqf_level, description, min_notional_hours, max_notional_hours, notional_hours_range, version, originally_approved, valid_till, awarding_body, certifying_bodies, proposed_occupation, progression_pathway, qualification_type, adopted_qualification, training_delivery_hours, is_pwd, pwd_categories, raw_metadata, source_file, is_active) VALUES ('NG-03-CO-02345-2024-V1-CSDCI', 'Plaster Mason - Advanced', 'construction', 'Construction', 3.0, 'A Plaster Mason is responsible for applying and finishing plaster on the interior and exterior surfaces of buildings. The person uses the relevant basic and advanced tools and equipment to create smooth, durable, and aesthetically pleasing finishes on walls and ceilings. The individual works as a small entrepreneur, setting up and managing a plaster masonry enterprise.', 120, 120, '1–200', 'Version', '15 Mar 2024', '15 Mar 2027', 'Construction Skill Development Council of India (CSDCI)', 'Construction Skill Development Council of India', 'N/A', 'N/A', 'General Qualification', 'N.A.', '{"Theory":"120","Practical":"00","EmployabilitySkills":"00","OJT_Mandatory":"00"}', false, '{}'::text[], '{"source_row": "41", "qualification_type": "General Qualification", "version": "Version"}'::jsonb, 'Qualifications 02-10-2026 20_02_11.xlsx', true) ON CONFLICT (q_code, title) DO UPDATE SET sector_id = EXCLUDED.sector_id, nsqf_level = EXCLUDED.nsqf_level, description = EXCLUDED.description, min_notional_hours = EXCLUDED.min_notional_hours, max_notional_hours = EXCLUDED.max_notional_hours, notional_hours_range = EXCLUDED.notional_hours_range, is_pwd = EXCLUDED.is_pwd, pwd_categories = EXCLUDED.pwd_categories, updated_at = NOW();
INSERT INTO nsqf_qualifications (q_code, title, sector_id, sector_name, nsqf_level, description, min_notional_hours, max_notional_hours, notional_hours_range, version, originally_approved, valid_till, awarding_body, certifying_bodies, proposed_occupation, progression_pathway, qualification_type, adopted_qualification, training_delivery_hours, is_pwd, pwd_categories, raw_metadata, source_file, is_active) VALUES ('NG-03-CO-02346-2024-V1-CSDCI', 'Tile Mason - Advanced', 'construction', 'Construction', 3.0, 'A Tile Mason is responsible for installing different types of tiles on surfaces in residential, commercial, and industrial settings using the appropriate basic and advanced tile masonry tools and equipment. The individual works as a small entrepreneur, setting up and managing a tile masonry enterprise.', 120, 120, '1–200', 'Version', '15 Mar 2024', '15 Mar 2027', 'Construction Skill Development Council of India (CSDCI)', 'Construction Skill Development Council of India', 'N/A', 'N/A', 'General Qualification', 'N.A.', '{"Theory":"120","Practical":"00","EmployabilitySkills":"00","OJT_Mandatory":"00"}', false, '{}'::text[], '{"source_row": "42", "qualification_type": "General Qualification", "version": "Version"}'::jsonb, 'Qualifications 02-10-2026 20_02_11.xlsx', true) ON CONFLICT (q_code, title) DO UPDATE SET sector_id = EXCLUDED.sector_id, nsqf_level = EXCLUDED.nsqf_level, description = EXCLUDED.description, min_notional_hours = EXCLUDED.min_notional_hours, max_notional_hours = EXCLUDED.max_notional_hours, notional_hours_range = EXCLUDED.notional_hours_range, is_pwd = EXCLUDED.is_pwd, pwd_categories = EXCLUDED.pwd_categories, updated_at = NOW();
INSERT INTO nsqf_qualifications (q_code, title, sector_id, sector_name, nsqf_level, description, min_notional_hours, max_notional_hours, notional_hours_range, version, originally_approved, valid_till, awarding_body, certifying_bodies, proposed_occupation, progression_pathway, qualification_type, adopted_qualification, training_delivery_hours, is_pwd, pwd_categories, raw_metadata, source_file, is_active) VALUES ('QG-4.5-CO-02391-2024-V1-MSME', 'Front Line Junior Supervisor (Construction)', 'construction', 'Construction', 4.5, 'Learners who attain this qualification are competent to work in Civil Construction and can get a job in a captive or commercial construction sector or become an entrepreneur.
•	Qualifying learners attain skills to work in Auto CAD, STADD PRO, 3D Studio MAX, REVIT, Adobe Photoshop, GPS , DGPS Auto Level & total station
•	Qualified learners are capable in Estimation and Costing related constructional work
•	Qualified learners are able to design civil constructional work by considering the strength of Civil Structure', 600, 600, '401–600', 'Version', '30 Apr 2024', '30 Apr 2027', 'MSME Technology Centre, Ministry of Micro Small And Medium Enterprises, New Delhi', 'MSME TECHNOLOGY CENTRE', 'Project Management (Structural Design and Analysis)', 'Project coordinator (Construction)', 'Cross Sectoral Qualification', 'N.A.', '{"Theory":"60","Practical":"420","EmployabilitySkills":"60","OJT_Mandatory":"60"}', false, '{}'::text[], '{"source_row": "43", "qualification_type": "Cross Sectoral Qualification", "version": "Version"}'::jsonb, 'Qualifications 02-10-2026 20_02_11.xlsx', true) ON CONFLICT (q_code, title) DO UPDATE SET sector_id = EXCLUDED.sector_id, nsqf_level = EXCLUDED.nsqf_level, description = EXCLUDED.description, min_notional_hours = EXCLUDED.min_notional_hours, max_notional_hours = EXCLUDED.max_notional_hours, notional_hours_range = EXCLUDED.notional_hours_range, is_pwd = EXCLUDED.is_pwd, pwd_categories = EXCLUDED.pwd_categories, updated_at = NOW();
INSERT INTO nsqf_qualifications (q_code, title, sector_id, sector_name, nsqf_level, description, min_notional_hours, max_notional_hours, notional_hours_range, version, originally_approved, valid_till, awarding_body, certifying_bodies, proposed_occupation, progression_pathway, qualification_type, adopted_qualification, training_delivery_hours, is_pwd, pwd_categories, raw_metadata, source_file, is_active) VALUES ('QG-5.5-CO-02392-2024-V1-MSME', 'PROJECT COORDINATOR (CONSTRUCTION)', 'construction', 'Construction', 5.5, 'Learners who attain this qualification are competent in Civil Construction work and can get a job in a captive or commercial construction work or become an entrepreneur and  Qualifying learners shall be able to : 
•	Work in Auto-CAD, STADD. Pro, 3Ds-Max & Sketch-Up, Estimation & Costing, Advance Survey, Soft Skill, Revit, Tekla, Arc-GIS, Primavera, Advance Road Design & Material Testing.
●	Carry out structural planning & designing, interior & exterior designing, estimation and costing related to constructional work.
●	Design civil constructional work by considering the strength of civil construction.
●	Coordinate the project management in different project works.', 1200, 1200, '1001–1200', 'Version', '30 Apr 2024', '30 Apr 2027', 'MSME Technology Centre, Ministry of Micro Small And Medium Enterprises, New Delhi', 'MSME TECHNOLOGY CENTRE', 'Project Management (Structural Design and Analysis)', 'Deputy Project Manager', 'General Qualification', 'N.A.', '{"Theory":"120","Practical":"840","EmployabilitySkills":"120","OJT_Mandatory":"120"}', false, '{}'::text[], '{"source_row": "44", "qualification_type": "General Qualification", "version": "Version"}'::jsonb, 'Qualifications 02-10-2026 20_02_11.xlsx', true) ON CONFLICT (q_code, title) DO UPDATE SET sector_id = EXCLUDED.sector_id, nsqf_level = EXCLUDED.nsqf_level, description = EXCLUDED.description, min_notional_hours = EXCLUDED.min_notional_hours, max_notional_hours = EXCLUDED.max_notional_hours, notional_hours_range = EXCLUDED.notional_hours_range, is_pwd = EXCLUDED.is_pwd, pwd_categories = EXCLUDED.pwd_categories, updated_at = NOW();
INSERT INTO nsqf_qualifications (q_code, title, sector_id, sector_name, nsqf_level, description, min_notional_hours, max_notional_hours, notional_hours_range, version, originally_approved, valid_till, awarding_body, certifying_bodies, proposed_occupation, progression_pathway, qualification_type, adopted_qualification, training_delivery_hours, is_pwd, pwd_categories, raw_metadata, source_file, is_active) VALUES ('ICE/CONS/24/Q1001', 'MEP Supervisor - Maintenance', 'construction', 'Construction', 5.0, 'MEP Supervisor - Maintenance supervises the Mechanical, Electrical and Plumbing (MEP) activities in the management of a building infrastructure. It includes electrical, plumbing and infrastructure maintenance.The individual also uses computer and applies appropriate IT skills in work. The person may optionally supervise the maintenance of the infrastructure and use of the Building Management System (BMS).', 510, 600, '401–600', 'Version', '30 May 2024', '29 May 2027', 'Integrated Council for Entrepreneurship and Skilling (ICES)', 'The Institution of Civil Engineers Society', 'Facility Management', 'MEP Site Engineer (L6)', 'Multi-Skill Qualification', 'N.A.', '{"Theory":"90","Practical":"180","EmployabilitySkills":"60","OJT_Mandatory":"180"}', false, '{}'::text[], '{"source_row": "45", "qualification_type": "Multi-Skill Qualification", "version": "Version"}'::jsonb, 'Qualifications 02-10-2026 20_02_11.xlsx', true) ON CONFLICT (q_code, title) DO UPDATE SET sector_id = EXCLUDED.sector_id, nsqf_level = EXCLUDED.nsqf_level, description = EXCLUDED.description, min_notional_hours = EXCLUDED.min_notional_hours, max_notional_hours = EXCLUDED.max_notional_hours, notional_hours_range = EXCLUDED.notional_hours_range, is_pwd = EXCLUDED.is_pwd, pwd_categories = EXCLUDED.pwd_categories, updated_at = NOW();
INSERT INTO nsqf_qualifications (q_code, title, sector_id, sector_name, nsqf_level, description, min_notional_hours, max_notional_hours, notional_hours_range, version, originally_approved, valid_till, awarding_body, certifying_bodies, proposed_occupation, progression_pathway, qualification_type, adopted_qualification, training_delivery_hours, is_pwd, pwd_categories, raw_metadata, source_file, is_active) VALUES ('QC-05-CO-02969-2024-V1-SSDF', 'Fire Safety Officer', 'construction', 'Construction', 5.0, 'A Fire Safety Officer is responsible for developing and implementing fire safety policies and procedures, identifying fire hazards, conducting fire risk assessments, training employees and ensuring safety of people and property against fire hazards. The officer is responsible to ensure compliance with fire safety regulations & codes, conduct fire safety inspection, investigate fire incidents, and develop emergency response plans, fire exits and fire drills.', 600, 600, '401–600', 'Version', '27 Aug 2024', '27 Aug 2027', 'Safety Skill Development Foundation', 'SAFETY SKILL DEVELOPMENT FOUNDATION', 'Fire  Safety Engineering & Management', 'Fire Safety Manager -Level  6,  Safety Consultant/Advisor-  Level 7,   Industrial Hygienist - Level  5', 'Apprenticeship Qualification,Cross Sectoral Qualification,General Qualification,Multi-Skill Qualification', 'N.A.', '{"Theory":"270","Practical":"180","EmployabilitySkills":"60","OJT_Mandatory":"90"}', false, '{}'::text[], '{"source_row": "46", "qualification_type": "Apprenticeship Qualification,Cross Sectoral Qualification,General Qualification,Multi-Skill Qualification", "version": "Version"}'::jsonb, 'Qualifications 02-10-2026 20_02_11.xlsx', true) ON CONFLICT (q_code, title) DO UPDATE SET sector_id = EXCLUDED.sector_id, nsqf_level = EXCLUDED.nsqf_level, description = EXCLUDED.description, min_notional_hours = EXCLUDED.min_notional_hours, max_notional_hours = EXCLUDED.max_notional_hours, notional_hours_range = EXCLUDED.notional_hours_range, is_pwd = EXCLUDED.is_pwd, pwd_categories = EXCLUDED.pwd_categories, updated_at = NOW();
INSERT INTO nsqf_qualifications (q_code, title, sector_id, sector_name, nsqf_level, description, min_notional_hours, max_notional_hours, notional_hours_range, version, originally_approved, valid_till, awarding_body, certifying_bodies, proposed_occupation, progression_pathway, qualification_type, adopted_qualification, training_delivery_hours, is_pwd, pwd_categories, raw_metadata, source_file, is_active) VALUES ('QC-05-CO-02970-2024-V1-SSDF', 'Electrical Safety Supervisor', 'construction', 'Construction', 5.0, 'The Electrical Safety Supervisor will be responsible to ensure safe operations of power systems. As an electrical supervisor, the professional will demonstrate strong understanding of electrical safety engineering practices, will ensure that all electrical work at the worksite is completed on time and in accordance with the rules and regulations implied in the industry. The Electrical Safety Supervisor is responsible for maintaining at par electrical safety in industries. The professional will contribute in designing and improving safety performance and in meeting the statutory requirements set by the governing bodies.', 600, 600, '401–600', 'Version', '27 Aug 2024', '27 Aug 2027', 'Safety Skill Development Foundation', 'SAFETY SKILL DEVELOPMENT FOUNDATION', 'Electrical Safety  Management', 'Electrical Safety Inspector-  Level  6, Electrical Safety Trainer - Level 5', 'Apprenticeship Qualification,Cross Sectoral Qualification,General Qualification,Multi-Skill Qualification', 'N.A.', '{"Theory":"270","Practical":"180","EmployabilitySkills":"60","OJT_Mandatory":"90"}', false, '{}'::text[], '{"source_row": "47", "qualification_type": "Apprenticeship Qualification,Cross Sectoral Qualification,General Qualification,Multi-Skill Qualification", "version": "Version"}'::jsonb, 'Qualifications 02-10-2026 20_02_11.xlsx', true) ON CONFLICT (q_code, title) DO UPDATE SET sector_id = EXCLUDED.sector_id, nsqf_level = EXCLUDED.nsqf_level, description = EXCLUDED.description, min_notional_hours = EXCLUDED.min_notional_hours, max_notional_hours = EXCLUDED.max_notional_hours, notional_hours_range = EXCLUDED.notional_hours_range, is_pwd = EXCLUDED.is_pwd, pwd_categories = EXCLUDED.pwd_categories, updated_at = NOW();
INSERT INTO nsqf_qualifications (q_code, title, sector_id, sector_name, nsqf_level, description, min_notional_hours, max_notional_hours, notional_hours_range, version, originally_approved, valid_till, awarding_body, certifying_bodies, proposed_occupation, progression_pathway, qualification_type, adopted_qualification, training_delivery_hours, is_pwd, pwd_categories, raw_metadata, source_file, is_active) VALUES ('QC-06-CO-02971-2024-V1-SSDF', 'Scaffold Design Engineer', 'construction', 'Construction', 6.0, 'A Scaffold Design Engineer is responsible for creating safe and efficient scaffold designs using industry standards and codes utilizes scaffold structural design software and computer-aided design (CAD) & systems to develop accurate scaffold drawings. The design engineer calculates loads in accordance with national & international standards and analyzes scaffold structures using design software like STAAD Pro software and have good understanding of scaffold specifications, drawings, Indian and international standard codes to ensure compliance and safety in scaffold designs.', 690, 690, '601–800', 'Version', '27 Aug 2024', '27 Aug 2027', 'Safety Skill Development Foundation', 'Safety Skill Development Foundation', 'Scaffolding Engineering & Management', 'Lead Scaffold Design Engineer (Level: 6.5), Scaffold Manager (Level: 7)', 'Apprenticeship Qualification,Cross Sectoral Qualification,General Qualification,Multi-Skill Qualification', 'N.A.', '{"Theory":"378","Practical":"132","EmployabilitySkills":"60","OJT_Mandatory":"120"}', false, '{}'::text[], '{"source_row": "48", "qualification_type": "Apprenticeship Qualification,Cross Sectoral Qualification,General Qualification,Multi-Skill Qualification", "version": "Version"}'::jsonb, 'Qualifications 02-10-2026 20_02_11.xlsx', true) ON CONFLICT (q_code, title) DO UPDATE SET sector_id = EXCLUDED.sector_id, nsqf_level = EXCLUDED.nsqf_level, description = EXCLUDED.description, min_notional_hours = EXCLUDED.min_notional_hours, max_notional_hours = EXCLUDED.max_notional_hours, notional_hours_range = EXCLUDED.notional_hours_range, is_pwd = EXCLUDED.is_pwd, pwd_categories = EXCLUDED.pwd_categories, updated_at = NOW();
INSERT INTO nsqf_qualifications (q_code, title, sector_id, sector_name, nsqf_level, description, min_notional_hours, max_notional_hours, notional_hours_range, version, originally_approved, valid_till, awarding_body, certifying_bodies, proposed_occupation, progression_pathway, qualification_type, adopted_qualification, training_delivery_hours, is_pwd, pwd_categories, raw_metadata, source_file, is_active) VALUES ('NM-04-CO-03004-2024-V1-SSDF', 'Basics of Occupational Hazards & Risk Management', 'construction', 'Construction', 4.0, 'The Micro Credential describes the various workplaces risks & hazards, their identification, and remedial steps to ensure safety at workplaces and risk management. The MC helps management staff in understanding occupational hazards and timely mitigation through planning & management.', 15, 15, '1–200', 'Version', '27 Aug 2024', '27 Aug 2027', 'Safety Skill Development Foundation', 'SAFETY SKILL DEVELOPMENT FOUNDATION', 'Occupational Safety Health & Environment (OSHE) Engineering & Management', 'N/A', 'Micro Credentials', 'N.A.', '{"Theory":"8","Practical":"7","EmployabilitySkills":"0","OJT_Mandatory":"0"}', false, '{}'::text[], '{"source_row": "49", "qualification_type": "Micro Credentials", "version": "Version"}'::jsonb, 'Qualifications 02-10-2026 20_02_11.xlsx', true) ON CONFLICT (q_code, title) DO UPDATE SET sector_id = EXCLUDED.sector_id, nsqf_level = EXCLUDED.nsqf_level, description = EXCLUDED.description, min_notional_hours = EXCLUDED.min_notional_hours, max_notional_hours = EXCLUDED.max_notional_hours, notional_hours_range = EXCLUDED.notional_hours_range, is_pwd = EXCLUDED.is_pwd, pwd_categories = EXCLUDED.pwd_categories, updated_at = NOW();
INSERT INTO nsqf_qualifications (q_code, title, sector_id, sector_name, nsqf_level, description, min_notional_hours, max_notional_hours, notional_hours_range, version, originally_approved, valid_till, awarding_body, certifying_bodies, proposed_occupation, progression_pathway, qualification_type, adopted_qualification, training_delivery_hours, is_pwd, pwd_categories, raw_metadata, source_file, is_active) VALUES ('NM-04-CO-03005-2024-V1-SSDF', 'Basics of Risk Analysis & Accident Prevention methods', 'construction', 'Construction', 4.0, 'The MC on Basics of Risk Analysis & Accident Prevention Methods describes the numerous measures considered as relevant for accident prevention, e.g. design and use of more safe equipment and technologies or replacing dangerous equipment and products by non-dangerous or less dangerous ones, improvement of working environment, use and maintenance of personal protective equipment, management and staff training, improvement of communication.', 15, 15, '1–200', 'Version', '27 Aug 2024', '27 Aug 2027', 'Safety Skill Development Foundation', 'Safety Skill Development Foundation', 'Occupational Safety Health & Environment (OSHE) Engineering & Management', 'N/A', 'Micro Credentials', 'N.A.', '{"Theory":"8","Practical":"7","EmployabilitySkills":"0","OJT_Mandatory":"0"}', false, '{}'::text[], '{"source_row": "50", "qualification_type": "Micro Credentials", "version": "Version"}'::jsonb, 'Qualifications 02-10-2026 20_02_11.xlsx', true) ON CONFLICT (q_code, title) DO UPDATE SET sector_id = EXCLUDED.sector_id, nsqf_level = EXCLUDED.nsqf_level, description = EXCLUDED.description, min_notional_hours = EXCLUDED.min_notional_hours, max_notional_hours = EXCLUDED.max_notional_hours, notional_hours_range = EXCLUDED.notional_hours_range, is_pwd = EXCLUDED.is_pwd, pwd_categories = EXCLUDED.pwd_categories, updated_at = NOW();
INSERT INTO nsqf_qualifications (q_code, title, sector_id, sector_name, nsqf_level, description, min_notional_hours, max_notional_hours, notional_hours_range, version, originally_approved, valid_till, awarding_body, certifying_bodies, proposed_occupation, progression_pathway, qualification_type, adopted_qualification, training_delivery_hours, is_pwd, pwd_categories, raw_metadata, source_file, is_active) VALUES ('NM-04-CO-03006-2024-V1-SSDF', 'Basics of Fire hazards & safety against fire hazards', 'construction', 'Construction', 4.0, 'The MC provides specialized knowledge in fire safety procedures aimed at minimizing fire damage. These encompass evaluation of potential fire risks and measures to prevent the outbreak of uncontrolled fire as well as strategies to contain and mitigate their impact. It also deals with necessary fire safety information, fire drills and compliances.', 7, 7, '1–200', 'Version', '27 Aug 2024', '27 Aug 2027', 'Safety Skill Development Foundation', 'Safety Skill Development Foundation', 'Fire Safety Engineering & Management', 'N/A', 'Micro Credentials', 'N.A.', '{"Theory":"4","Practical":"3.5","EmployabilitySkills":"0","OJT_Mandatory":"0"}', false, '{}'::text[], '{"source_row": "51", "qualification_type": "Micro Credentials", "version": "Version"}'::jsonb, 'Qualifications 02-10-2026 20_02_11.xlsx', true) ON CONFLICT (q_code, title) DO UPDATE SET sector_id = EXCLUDED.sector_id, nsqf_level = EXCLUDED.nsqf_level, description = EXCLUDED.description, min_notional_hours = EXCLUDED.min_notional_hours, max_notional_hours = EXCLUDED.max_notional_hours, notional_hours_range = EXCLUDED.notional_hours_range, is_pwd = EXCLUDED.is_pwd, pwd_categories = EXCLUDED.pwd_categories, updated_at = NOW();
INSERT INTO nsqf_qualifications (q_code, title, sector_id, sector_name, nsqf_level, description, min_notional_hours, max_notional_hours, notional_hours_range, version, originally_approved, valid_till, awarding_body, certifying_bodies, proposed_occupation, progression_pathway, qualification_type, adopted_qualification, training_delivery_hours, is_pwd, pwd_categories, raw_metadata, source_file, is_active) VALUES ('NM-04-CO-03007-2024-V1-SSDF', 'Basics of Safety & Health Requirement of BOCW Act 1996', 'construction', 'Construction', 4.0, 'The Micro Credential brings out details of safety & health measures to be ensured at workplaces and statutory compliance requirements as per the BOCW Act 1996. It also provides the details of welfare measures, committees and license requirements as per the Act.', 7, 7, '1–200', 'Version', '27 Aug 2024', '27 Aug 2027', 'Safety Skill Development Foundation', 'Safety Skill Development Foundation', 'Construction Engineering & Management', 'N/A', 'Micro Credentials', 'N.A.', '{"Theory":"4","Practical":"3.5","EmployabilitySkills":"0","OJT_Mandatory":"0"}', false, '{}'::text[], '{"source_row": "52", "qualification_type": "Micro Credentials", "version": "Version"}'::jsonb, 'Qualifications 02-10-2026 20_02_11.xlsx', true) ON CONFLICT (q_code, title) DO UPDATE SET sector_id = EXCLUDED.sector_id, nsqf_level = EXCLUDED.nsqf_level, description = EXCLUDED.description, min_notional_hours = EXCLUDED.min_notional_hours, max_notional_hours = EXCLUDED.max_notional_hours, notional_hours_range = EXCLUDED.notional_hours_range, is_pwd = EXCLUDED.is_pwd, pwd_categories = EXCLUDED.pwd_categories, updated_at = NOW();
INSERT INTO nsqf_qualifications (q_code, title, sector_id, sector_name, nsqf_level, description, min_notional_hours, max_notional_hours, notional_hours_range, version, originally_approved, valid_till, awarding_body, certifying_bodies, proposed_occupation, progression_pathway, qualification_type, adopted_qualification, training_delivery_hours, is_pwd, pwd_categories, raw_metadata, source_file, is_active) VALUES ('NM-2.5-CO-03008-2024-V1-SSDF', 'Basics of Safety Protocols for Construction Works', 'construction', 'Construction', 2.5, 'The Micro credential provides the safety protocols, process required to be followed and personal protective equipment (PPEs) to be used by the workers at construction site while performing various construction activities at height, at elevated platforms, depths, handling materials and precautions to be taken  while moving at the construction site and maintaining a tidy work-site environment.', 15, 15, '1–200', 'Version', '27 Aug 2024', '27 Aug 2027', 'Safety Skill Development Foundation', 'Safety Skill Development Foundation', 'Construction Engineering & Management', 'N/A', 'Micro Credentials', 'N.A.', '{"Theory":"8","Practical":"7","EmployabilitySkills":"0","OJT_Mandatory":"0"}', false, '{}'::text[], '{"source_row": "53", "qualification_type": "Micro Credentials", "version": "Version"}'::jsonb, 'Qualifications 02-10-2026 20_02_11.xlsx', true) ON CONFLICT (q_code, title) DO UPDATE SET sector_id = EXCLUDED.sector_id, nsqf_level = EXCLUDED.nsqf_level, description = EXCLUDED.description, min_notional_hours = EXCLUDED.min_notional_hours, max_notional_hours = EXCLUDED.max_notional_hours, notional_hours_range = EXCLUDED.notional_hours_range, is_pwd = EXCLUDED.is_pwd, pwd_categories = EXCLUDED.pwd_categories, updated_at = NOW();
