step-by-step guide to conducting effective audits within the food processing industry.', 15, 15, '1–200', 'Version', '08 May 2025', '07 May 2028', 'Food Industry Capacity & Skill Initiative (FICSI)', 'Food Industry Capacity and Skill Initiative (FICSI)', 'Quality Analysis/ Assurance', 'None', 'General Qualification', 'N.A.', '{"Theory":"08.00","Practical":"07.00","EmployabilitySkills":"00.00","OJT_Mandatory":"00.00"}', false, '{}'::text[], '{"source_row": "43", "qualification_type": "General Qualification", "version": "Version"}'::jsonb, 'Qualifications 02-10-2026 20_06_01.xlsx', true) ON CONFLICT (q_code, title) DO UPDATE SET sector_id = EXCLUDED.sector_id, nsqf_level = EXCLUDED.nsqf_level, description = EXCLUDED.description, min_notional_hours = EXCLUDED.min_notional_hours, max_notional_hours = EXCLUDED.max_notional_hours, notional_hours_range = EXCLUDED.notional_hours_range, is_pwd = EXCLUDED.is_pwd, pwd_categories = EXCLUDED.pwd_categories, updated_at = NOW();
INSERT INTO nsqf_qualifications (q_code, title, sector_id, sector_name, nsqf_level, description, min_notional_hours, max_notional_hours, notional_hours_range, version, originally_approved, valid_till, awarding_body, certifying_bodies, proposed_occupation, progression_pathway, qualification_type, adopted_qualification, training_delivery_hours, is_pwd, pwd_categories, raw_metadata, source_file, is_active) VALUES ('NQR Code-NM-04-FI-04215-2025-V1-FICSI', 'Fundamentals of HACCP Implementation- Food Industry', 'food-industry-food-processing', 'Food Industry/Food Processing', 4.0, 'This course provides an introduction to the fundamentals of HACCP and its implementation in the food processing industry. Participants will learn the key principles of the HACCP system and how to apply them to ensure food safety and compliance with industry standards.', 15, 15, '1–200', 'Version', '08 May 2025', '07 May 2028', 'Food Industry Capacity & Skill Initiative (FICSI)', 'Food Industry Capacity and Skill Initiative (FICSI)', 'Quality Analysis/Assurance', 'Not Applicable', 'General Qualification,Micro Credentials,Upskilling Qualification', 'N.A.', '{"Theory":"9","Practical":"6","EmployabilitySkills":"0","OJT_Mandatory":"0"}', false, '{}'::text[], '{"source_row": "44", "qualification_type": "General Qualification,Micro Credentials,Upskilling Qualification", "version": "Version"}'::jsonb, 'Qualifications 02-10-2026 20_06_01.xlsx', true) ON CONFLICT (q_code, title) DO UPDATE SET sector_id = EXCLUDED.sector_id, nsqf_level = EXCLUDED.nsqf_level, description = EXCLUDED.description, min_notional_hours = EXCLUDED.min_notional_hours, max_notional_hours = EXCLUDED.max_notional_hours, notional_hours_range = EXCLUDED.notional_hours_range, is_pwd = EXCLUDED.is_pwd, pwd_categories = EXCLUDED.pwd_categories, updated_at = NOW();
INSERT INTO nsqf_qualifications (q_code, title, sector_id, sector_name, nsqf_level, description, min_notional_hours, max_notional_hours, notional_hours_range, version, originally_approved, valid_till, awarding_body, certifying_bodies, proposed_occupation, progression_pathway, qualification_type, adopted_qualification, training_delivery_hours, is_pwd, pwd_categories, raw_metadata, source_file, is_active) VALUES ('NQR CODE- QG-04-FI-04210-2025-V1-FICSI', 'Sales Associate- Food Industry', 'food-industry-food-processing', 'Food Industry/Food Processing', 4.0, 'The Food Sales Executive is responsible for driving sales, identifying and securing orders for food products and services, while maintaining strong client relationships. S/he will utilize their expertise to develop and execute effective sales strategies, negotiate contracts, and coordinate logistics to ensure timely delivery. Additionally, they will stay abreast of market trends and adapt their approach to maximize sales opportunities.', 450, 450, '401–600', 'Version', '08 May 2025', '07 May 2028', 'Food Industry Capacity & Skill Initiative (FICSI)', 'Food Industry Capacity and Skill Initiative (FICSI)', 'Food Sales and Retail Operations', 'Area Sales Manager (Level 5)', 'General Qualification', 'N.A.', '{"Theory":"120","Practical":"210","EmployabilitySkills":"60","OJT_Mandatory":"60"}', false, '{}'::text[], '{"source_row": "45", "qualification_type": "General Qualification", "version": "Version"}'::jsonb, 'Qualifications 02-10-2026 20_06_01.xlsx', true) ON CONFLICT (q_code, title) DO UPDATE SET sector_id = EXCLUDED.sector_id, nsqf_level = EXCLUDED.nsqf_level, description = EXCLUDED.description, min_notional_hours = EXCLUDED.min_notional_hours, max_notional_hours = EXCLUDED.max_notional_hours, notional_hours_range = EXCLUDED.notional_hours_range, is_pwd = EXCLUDED.is_pwd, pwd_categories = EXCLUDED.pwd_categories, updated_at = NOW();
INSERT INTO nsqf_qualifications (q_code, title, sector_id, sector_name, nsqf_level, description, min_notional_hours, max_notional_hours, notional_hours_range, version, originally_approved, valid_till, awarding_body, certifying_bodies, proposed_occupation, progression_pathway, qualification_type, adopted_qualification, training_delivery_hours, is_pwd, pwd_categories, raw_metadata, source_file, is_active) VALUES ('QG-03-FI-03328-2024-V4-FICSI.', 'Assistant Sorter and Grader - Fruits and Vegetables', 'food-industry-food-processing', 'Food Industry/Food Processing', 3.0, 'An Assistant Sorter and Grader - Fruits and Vegetables is responsible for sorting and grading
different types of produce, including fruits and vegetables, based on applicable parameters. The
individual also packs and stores the produce before it is dispatched to the buyers and markets.', 300, 300, '201–400', 'Version', '22 Oct 2024', '22 Oct 2027', 'Food Industry Capacity & Skill Initiative (FICSI)', 'Food Industry Capacity and Skill Initiative (FICSI)', 'Sorting and Grading', 'Preservation Technician', 'General Qualification,Upskilling Qualification', 'N.A.', '{"Theory":"60","Practical":"150","EmployabilitySkills":"30","OJT_Mandatory":"60"}', false, '{}'::text[], '{"source_row": "46", "qualification_type": "General Qualification,Upskilling Qualification", "version": "Version"}'::jsonb, 'Qualifications 02-10-2026 20_06_01.xlsx', true) ON CONFLICT (q_code, title) DO UPDATE SET sector_id = EXCLUDED.sector_id, nsqf_level = EXCLUDED.nsqf_level, description = EXCLUDED.description, min_notional_hours = EXCLUDED.min_notional_hours, max_notional_hours = EXCLUDED.max_notional_hours, notional_hours_range = EXCLUDED.notional_hours_range, is_pwd = EXCLUDED.is_pwd, pwd_categories = EXCLUDED.pwd_categories, updated_at = NOW();
INSERT INTO nsqf_qualifications (q_code, title, sector_id, sector_name, nsqf_level, description, min_notional_hours, max_notional_hours, notional_hours_range, version, originally_approved, valid_till, awarding_body, certifying_bodies, proposed_occupation, progression_pathway, qualification_type, adopted_qualification, training_delivery_hours, is_pwd, pwd_categories, raw_metadata, source_file, is_active) VALUES ('QG-04-FI-03893-2025-V2-FICSI.', 'Processed Food Entrepreneur', 'food-industry-food-processing', 'Food Industry/Food Processing', 4.0, 'A Processed Food Entrepreneur is responsible for establishing and managing a food processing business by identifying market opportunities, innovating products, and enhancing their value. They focus on developing unique food products, optimizing operations, and driving profitability through strategic market exploration and business growth.', 480, 480, '401–600', 'Version', '18 Feb 2025', '17 Feb 2028', 'Food Industry Capacity & Skill Initiative (FICSI)', 'Food Industry Capacity and Skill Initiative (FICSI)', 'Entrepreneur', 'Supervisor-Food Processing Industries (Level 5)', 'General Qualification', 'N.A.', '{"Theory":"120","Practical":"210","EmployabilitySkills":"30","OJT_Mandatory":"120"}', false, '{}'::text[], '{"source_row": "47", "qualification_type": "General Qualification", "version": "Version"}'::jsonb, 'Qualifications 02-10-2026 20_06_01.xlsx', true) ON CONFLICT (q_code, title) DO UPDATE SET sector_id = EXCLUDED.sector_id, nsqf_level = EXCLUDED.nsqf_level, description = EXCLUDED.description, min_notional_hours = EXCLUDED.min_notional_hours, max_notional_hours = EXCLUDED.max_notional_hours, notional_hours_range = EXCLUDED.notional_hours_range, is_pwd = EXCLUDED.is_pwd, pwd_categories = EXCLUDED.pwd_categories, updated_at = NOW();
INSERT INTO nsqf_qualifications (q_code, title, sector_id, sector_name, nsqf_level, description, min_notional_hours, max_notional_hours, notional_hours_range, version, originally_approved, valid_till, awarding_body, certifying_bodies, proposed_occupation, progression_pathway, qualification_type, adopted_qualification, training_delivery_hours, is_pwd, pwd_categories, raw_metadata, source_file, is_active) VALUES ('QG-03-FI-03331-2024-V4-FICSI.', 'Grain Miller', 'food-industry-food-processing', 'Food Industry/Food Processing', 3.0, 'A Grain Miller is responsible for operating and maintaining milling equipment used for processing wheat, pulses, or cereals under supervision. This includes tasks such as setting up machinery, adjusting controls for optimal milling, and conducting routine inspections to ensure product quality and consistency. The role also involves post-production cleaning, basic maintenance, and adhering to food safety and hygiene standards to ensure efficient and safe operations.', 360, 450, '401–600', 'Version', '22 Oct 2024', '21 Oct 2027', 'Food Industry Capacity & Skill Initiative (FICSI)', 'Food Industry Capacity and Skill Initiative (FICSI)', 'Flour Mill Operator', 'Supervisor Milling', 'General Qualification', 'N.A.', '{"Theory":"120","Practical":"180","EmployabilitySkills":"30","OJT_Mandatory":"30"}', false, '{}'::text[], '{"source_row": "48", "qualification_type": "General Qualification", "version": "Version"}'::jsonb, 'Qualifications 02-10-2026 20_06_01.xlsx', true) ON CONFLICT (q_code, title) DO UPDATE SET sector_id = EXCLUDED.sector_id, nsqf_level = EXCLUDED.nsqf_level, description = EXCLUDED.description, min_notional_hours = EXCLUDED.min_notional_hours, max_notional_hours = EXCLUDED.max_notional_hours, notional_hours_range = EXCLUDED.notional_hours_range, is_pwd = EXCLUDED.is_pwd, pwd_categories = EXCLUDED.pwd_categories, updated_at = NOW();
INSERT INTO nsqf_qualifications (q_code, title, sector_id, sector_name, nsqf_level, description, min_notional_hours, max_notional_hours, notional_hours_range, version, originally_approved, valid_till, awarding_body, certifying_bodies, proposed_occupation, progression_pathway, qualification_type, adopted_qualification, training_delivery_hours, is_pwd, pwd_categories, raw_metadata, source_file, is_active) VALUES ('QG-03-FI-03998-2025-V2-FICSI.', 'Spice Processor', 'food-industry-food-processing', 'Food Industry/Food Processing', 3.0, 'A Spice Processor is responsible for processing a variety of whole and powdered spices, as well as seasonings, by efficiently operating and synchronizing different tools, machinery, and automated systems. They ensure seamless production by adhering to Standard Operating Procedures (SOPs) while maintaining consistency in quality and output. The role also involves conducting regular quality checks, monitoring critical control points, and leveraging automation to enhance efficiency, minimize contamination risks, and optimize the overall production process.', 360, 360, '201–400', 'Version', '01 May 2025', '30 Apr 2028', 'Food Industry Capacity & Skill Initiative (FICSI)', 'Food Industry Capacity and Skill Initiative (FICSI)', 'Processing-Packaged Foods', 'Processing - Packaged Foods (L4)', 'General Qualification,Upskilling Qualification', 'N.A.', '{"Theory":"90","Practical":"180","EmployabilitySkills":"30","OJT_Mandatory":"60"}', false, '{}'::text[], '{"source_row": "49", "qualification_type": "General Qualification,Upskilling Qualification", "version": "Version"}'::jsonb, 'Qualifications 02-10-2026 20_06_01.xlsx', true) ON CONFLICT (q_code, title) DO UPDATE SET sector_id = EXCLUDED.sector_id, nsqf_level = EXCLUDED.nsqf_level, description = EXCLUDED.description, min_notional_hours = EXCLUDED.min_notional_hours, max_notional_hours = EXCLUDED.max_notional_hours, notional_hours_range = EXCLUDED.notional_hours_range, is_pwd = EXCLUDED.is_pwd, pwd_categories = EXCLUDED.pwd_categories, updated_at = NOW();
INSERT INTO nsqf_qualifications (q_code, title, sector_id, sector_name, nsqf_level, description, min_notional_hours, max_notional_hours, notional_hours_range, version, originally_approved, valid_till, awarding_body, certifying_bodies, proposed_occupation, progression_pathway, qualification_type, adopted_qualification, training_delivery_hours, is_pwd, pwd_categories, raw_metadata, source_file, is_active) VALUES ('QG-2.5-FI-04209-2025-V1-FICSI.', 'Food Handling and Service Assistant', 'food-industry-food-processing', 'Food Industry/Food Processing', 2.5, 'A Food Handling and Service Assistant is responsible for delivering prompt and friendly customer service, accurately handling orders and cash transactions, preparing food items per standard recipes, safely operating kitchen equipment, ensuring adherence to food safety standards, and assisting in efficient inventory management. The role demands high-volume production capabilities and effective customer interaction in a fast-paced environment.', 240, 240, '201–400', 'Version', '08 May 2025', '07 May 2028', 'Food Industry Capacity & Skill Initiative (FICSI)', 'Food Industry Capacity and Skill Initiative (FICSI)', 'Food Production and Kitchen', 'Food Production and Service in-charge (L3.5)', 'General Qualification,Upskilling Qualification', 'N.A.', '{"Theory":"60","Practical":"120","EmployabilitySkills":"30","OJT_Mandatory":"30"}', false, '{}'::text[], '{"source_row": "50", "qualification_type": "General Qualification,Upskilling Qualification", "version": "Version"}'::jsonb, 'Qualifications 02-10-2026 20_06_01.xlsx', true) ON CONFLICT (q_code, title) DO UPDATE SET sector_id = EXCLUDED.sector_id, nsqf_level = EXCLUDED.nsqf_level, description = EXCLUDED.description, min_notional_hours = EXCLUDED.min_notional_hours, max_notional_hours = EXCLUDED.max_notional_hours, notional_hours_range = EXCLUDED.notional_hours_range, is_pwd = EXCLUDED.is_pwd, pwd_categories = EXCLUDED.pwd_categories, updated_at = NOW();
INSERT INTO nsqf_qualifications (q_code, title, sector_id, sector_name, nsqf_level, description, min_notional_hours, max_notional_hours, notional_hours_range, version, originally_approved, valid_till, awarding_body, certifying_bodies, proposed_occupation, progression_pathway, qualification_type, adopted_qualification, training_delivery_hours, is_pwd, pwd_categories, raw_metadata, source_file, is_active) VALUES ('NM-03-FI-04216-2025-V1-FICSI', 'Fundamentals of FSSAI Guidelines- Labelling & Display', 'food-industry-food-processing', 'Food Industry/Food Processing', 3.0, 'This micro-credential offers an in-depth understanding of labeling and display regulations. It covers FSSAI labeling guidelines, food label standards management, and display requirements. Participants will develop essential skills in regulatory compliance, precise label design, and effective product display strategies, ensuring compliance with standards and enhancing product integrity.', 7, 7, '1–200', 'Version', '08 May 2025', '07 May 2028', 'Food Industry Capacity & Skill Initiative (FICSI)', 'Food Industry Capacity and Skill Initiative (FICSI)', 'Quality Analysis/Assurance', 'Not Applicable', 'Micro Credentials,Upskilling Qualification', 'N.A.', '{"Theory":"04.30","Practical":"03.00","EmployabilitySkills":"0","OJT_Mandatory":"0"}', false, '{}'::text[], '{"source_row": "51", "qualification_type": "Micro Credentials,Upskilling Qualification", "version": "Version"}'::jsonb, 'Qualifications 02-10-2026 20_06_01.xlsx', true) ON CONFLICT (q_code, title) DO UPDATE SET sector_id = EXCLUDED.sector_id, nsqf_level = EXCLUDED.nsqf_level, description = EXCLUDED.description, min_notional_hours = EXCLUDED.min_notional_hours, max_notional_hours = EXCLUDED.max_notional_hours, notional_hours_range = EXCLUDED.notional_hours_range, is_pwd = EXCLUDED.is_pwd, pwd_categories = EXCLUDED.pwd_categories, updated_at = NOW();
INSERT INTO nsqf_qualifications (q_code, title, sector_id, sector_name, nsqf_level, description, min_notional_hours, max_notional_hours, notional_hours_range, version, originally_approved, valid_till, awarding_body, certifying_bodies, proposed_occupation, progression_pathway, qualification_type, adopted_qualification, training_delivery_hours, is_pwd, pwd_categories, raw_metadata, source_file, is_active) VALUES ('NG-04-FI-045142025-V1-FICSI', 'Fundamentals of Baking', 'food-industry-food-processing', 'Food Industry/Food Processing', 4.0, 'This course equips learners with essential baking skills and entrepreneurial knowledge, enabling them to successfully start and manage a home-based bakery business.', 60, 60, '1–200', 'Version', '07 Oct 2025', '06 Oct 2028', 'Food Industry Capacity & Skill Initiative (FICSI)', 'Sector Skill Council for Food Processing (FICSI)', 'Processing-Bread and Bakery', 'Not Applicable', 'General Qualification,National Occupational Standard', 'N.A.', '{"Theory":"20","Practical":"40","EmployabilitySkills":"0","OJT_Mandatory":"0"}', false, '{}'::text[], '{"source_row": "52", "qualification_type": "General Qualification,National Occupational Standard", "version": "Version"}'::jsonb, 'Qualifications 02-10-2026 20_06_01.xlsx', true) ON CONFLICT (q_code, title) DO UPDATE SET sector_id = EXCLUDED.sector_id, nsqf_level = EXCLUDED.nsqf_level, description = EXCLUDED.description, min_notional_hours = EXCLUDED.min_notional_hours, max_notional_hours = EXCLUDED.max_notional_hours, notional_hours_range = EXCLUDED.notional_hours_range, is_pwd = EXCLUDED.is_pwd, pwd_categories = EXCLUDED.pwd_categories, updated_at = NOW();
INSERT INTO nsqf_qualifications (q_code, title, sector_id, sector_name, nsqf_level, description, min_notional_hours, max_notional_hours, notional_hours_range, version, originally_approved, valid_till, awarding_body, certifying_bodies, proposed_occupation, progression_pathway, qualification_type, adopted_qualification, training_delivery_hours, is_pwd, pwd_categories, raw_metadata, source_file, is_active) VALUES ('QG-03-FI-03999-2025-V2-FICSI', 'Traditional sweet and savoury product maker', 'food-industry-food-processing', 'Food Industry/Food Processing', 3.0, 'A Traditional Sweet and Savoury Product Maker is responsible for making various types of sweet and savoury snack products. The individual is responsible for using their skills to carry out day to day activities in preparing variety of food items while meeting defined SOPs.', 300, 300, '201–400', 'Version', '01 May 2025', '30 Apr 2028', 'Food Industry Capacity & Skill Initiative (FICSI)', 'Food Industry Capacity & Skill Initiative (FICSI)', 'Processing-Packaged Foods', 'Convenience Food Maker (NSQF Level 4)', 'General Qualification,Upskilling Qualification', 'N.A.', '{"Theory":"60","Practical":"150","EmployabilitySkills":"30","OJT_Mandatory":"60"}', false, '{}'::text[], '{"source_row": "53", "qualification_type": "General Qualification,Upskilling Qualification", "version": "Version"}'::jsonb, 'Qualifications 02-10-2026 20_06_01.xlsx', true) ON CONFLICT (q_code, title) DO UPDATE SET sector_id = EXCLUDED.sector_id, nsqf_level = EXCLUDED.nsqf_level, description = EXCLUDED.description, min_notional_hours = EXCLUDED.min_notional_hours, max_notional_hours = EXCLUDED.max_notional_hours, notional_hours_range = EXCLUDED.notional_hours_range, is_pwd = EXCLUDED.is_pwd, pwd_categories = EXCLUDED.pwd_categories, updated_at = NOW();
INSERT INTO nsqf_qualifications (q_code, title, sector_id, sector_name, nsqf_level, description, min_notional_hours, max_notional_hours, notional_hours_range, version, originally_approved, valid_till, awarding_body, certifying_bodies, proposed_occupation, progression_pathway, qualification_type, adopted_qualification, training_delivery_hours, is_pwd, pwd_categories, raw_metadata, source_file, is_active) VALUES ('NG-2.5-GJ-00751-2023-V1-GJSCI', 'Goldsmith(sunar)', 'gem-jewellery', 'Gem & Jewellery', 2.5, '"Goldsmith (Sunar) is the name of the community and is derived from the word Sona meaning Gold
and people who work with gold are called Sunar or Sonar or Swarnkar or Goldsmiths or Silversmiths.
A Sunar or Goldsmith is a metalworker who specializes in working with precious metals like Gold
and silver. Historically they not only specialize in jewellery making but also in silverware, platters,
goblets, decorative utensils, etc.
They are skilled in making jewellery or ornaments using handmade precious metal forming and
finishing processes like filing, sawing, sawing, soldering, polishing, etc. These hand skills are included
in our job role or trade named, Jewellery Frame and Component Maker."', 40, 40, '1–200', 'Version', '11 Mar 2024', '11 Mar 2024', 'Gems & Jewellery Skill Council of India', 'Gems & Jewellery Skill Council of India', 'Gold smithy', 'Jewellery Frame and Component Maker, Goldsmith (Sunar), Entrepreneur', 'Upskilling Qualification', 'N.A.', 'N.A.', false, '{}'::text[], '{"source_row": "1", "qualification_type": "Upskilling Qualification", "version": "Version"}'::jsonb, 'Qualifications 02-10-2026 20_06_13.xlsx', true) ON CONFLICT (q_code, title) DO UPDATE SET sector_id = EXCLUDED.sector_id, nsqf_level = EXCLUDED.nsqf_level, description = EXCLUDED.description, min_notional_hours = EXCLUDED.min_notional_hours, max_notional_hours = EXCLUDED.max_notional_hours, notional_hours_range = EXCLUDED.notional_hours_range, is_pwd = EXCLUDED.is_pwd, pwd_categories = EXCLUDED.pwd_categories, updated_at = NOW();
INSERT INTO nsqf_qualifications (q_code, title, sector_id, sector_name, nsqf_level, description, min_notional_hours, max_notional_hours, notional_hours_range, version, originally_approved, valid_till, awarding_body, certifying_bodies, proposed_occupation, progression_pathway, qualification_type, adopted_qualification, training_delivery_hours, is_pwd, pwd_categories, raw_metadata, source_file, is_active) VALUES ('QG-4.5-GJ-01795-2024-V1-GJSCI', 'Jewellery_Version 1.0', 'gem-jewellery', 'Gem & Jewellery', 4.5, 'Jeweler fabricate and repair various jewellery articles. They create models from wax or metal and they may undertake the casting process (place wax model in casting ring, create moulds, pour molten metal into mould, or operate centrifugal casting machine to cast articles). Jeweler’s also cut, saw, file, and solder pieces of jewellery together, using a soldering torch, carving tools and hand tools and polish the article. The individual works with machine and hand tools to create jewellery components such as wire, strips etc. and frames from precious metal as per the design of jewellery pieces and articles. Individual can make exclusive jewellery pieces for use, pieces ready to be set with precious gemstones', 510, 510, '401–600', 'Version', '06 Feb 2024', '06 Feb 2026', 'Gems & Jewellery Skill Council of India', 'Gem & Jewellery Skill Council of India 
                                   Business Facilitation Centre, 4rth Floor, Special Economic Zone, Andheri (E). Mumbai 400 096', 'Goldsmith, Component Making/Filling/Assembling', 'Master or Repair Goldsmith/ Jeweler or Supervisor', 'General Qualification', 'N.A.', '{"Theory":"55","Practical":"95","EmployabilitySkills":"00","OJT_Mandatory":"360"}', false, '{}'::text[], '{"source_row": "2", "qualification_type": "General Qualification", "version": "Version"}'::jsonb, 'Qualifications 02-10-2026 20_06_13.xlsx', true) ON CONFLICT (q_code, title) DO UPDATE SET sector_id = EXCLUDED.sector_id, nsqf_level = EXCLUDED.nsqf_level, description = EXCLUDED.description, min_notional_hours = EXCLUDED.min_notional_hours, max_notional_hours = EXCLUDED.max_notional_hours, notional_hours_range = EXCLUDED.notional_hours_range, is_pwd = EXCLUDED.is_pwd, pwd_categories = EXCLUDED.pwd_categories, updated_at = NOW();
INSERT INTO nsqf_qualifications (q_code, title, sector_id, sector_name, nsqf_level, description, min_notional_hours, max_notional_hours, notional_hours_range, version, originally_approved, valid_till, awarding_body, certifying_bodies, proposed_occupation, progression_pathway, qualification_type, adopted_qualification, training_delivery_hours, is_pwd, pwd_categories, raw_metadata, source_file, is_active) VALUES ('NG-03-GJ-02342-2024-V1-GJSCI', 'Goldsmith (Sunar)- Advance', 'gem-jewellery', 'Gem & Jewellery', 3.0, 'Goldsmith (Sunar) is the name of the community and is derived from the word Sona meaning Gold and people who work with gold are called Sunar or Sonar or Swarnkar or Goldsmiths or Silversmiths. A Varishtha Sunar or Senior Goldsmith is a metalworker who specializes in working with precious metals like Gold and silver. Goldsmith (Sunar) is proficient in making intricate jewellery pieces using complex finishing or decorating techniques or processes like Mass finishing, plating, etc.', 120, 120, '1–200', 'Version', '15 Mar 2024', '15 Mar 2027', 'Gems & Jewellery Skill Council of India', 'Gem &Jewellery Skill Council of India  
                                     Business Facilitation Centre, 4th Floor, Special Economic Zone, Andheri (E). Mumbai 400 096', 'N/A', 'N/A', 'General Qualification', 'N.A.', '{"Theory":"120","Practical":"00","EmployabilitySkills":"00","OJT_Mandatory":"00"}', false, '{}'::text[], '{"source_row": "3", "qualification_type": "General Qualification", "version": "Version"}'::jsonb, 'Qualifications 02-10-2026 20_06_13.xlsx', true) ON CONFLICT (q_code, title) DO UPDATE SET sector_id = EXCLUDED.sector_id, nsqf_level = EXCLUDED.nsqf_level, description = EXCLUDED.description, min_notional_hours = EXCLUDED.min_notional_hours, max_notional_hours = EXCLUDED.max_notional_hours, notional_hours_range = EXCLUDED.notional_hours_range, is_pwd = EXCLUDED.is_pwd, pwd_categories = EXCLUDED.pwd_categories, updated_at = NOW();
INSERT INTO nsqf_qualifications (q_code, title, sector_id, sector_name, nsqf_level, description, min_notional_hours, max_notional_hours, notional_hours_range, version, originally_approved, valid_till, awarding_body, certifying_bodies, proposed_occupation, progression_pathway, qualification_type, adopted_qualification, training_delivery_hours, is_pwd, pwd_categories, raw_metadata, source_file, is_active) VALUES ('QG-02-GJ-03611-2025-V1-GJSCI', 'Imitation Jewellery Maker', 'gem-jewellery', 'Gem & Jewellery', 2.0, 'The Imitation Jewellery Maker must be creative, detail-oriented, and capable of working with delicate materials and intricate designs. Additionally, the job requires the individual to have basic communication skills, the ability to work in a team, and a commitment to maintaining personal hygiene and safety standards while working in a jewellery-making environment.', 270, 390, '201–400', 'Version', '18 Feb 2025', '28 Feb 2028', 'Gems & Jewellery Skill Council of India', 'Gem and Jewellery Skill Council of India', 'Component Making/Filling/Assembling, Metal
Alloying and Rolling', 'Imitation Jewellery Maker > Entrepreneur', 'General Qualification', 'N.A.', '{"Theory":"60","Practical":"150","EmployabilitySkills":"60","OJT_Mandatory":"0"}', false, '{}'::text[], '{"source_row": "4", "qualification_type": "General Qualification", "version": "Version"}'::jsonb, 'Qualifications 02-10-2026 20_06_13.xlsx', true) ON CONFLICT (q_code, title) DO UPDATE SET sector_id = EXCLUDED.sector_id, nsqf_level = EXCLUDED.nsqf_level, description = EXCLUDED.description, min_notional_hours = EXCLUDED.min_notional_hours, max_notional_hours = EXCLUDED.max_notional_hours, notional_hours_range = EXCLUDED.notional_hours_range, is_pwd = EXCLUDED.is_pwd, pwd_categories = EXCLUDED.pwd_categories, updated_at = NOW();
INSERT INTO nsqf_qualifications (q_code, title, sector_id, sector_name, nsqf_level, description, min_notional_hours, max_notional_hours, notional_hours_range, version, originally_approved, valid_till, awarding_body, certifying_bodies, proposed_occupation, progression_pathway, qualification_type, adopted_qualification, training_delivery_hours, is_pwd, pwd_categories, raw_metadata, source_file, is_active) VALUES ('QG-04-GC-04164-2025-V1-MSMETC', 'Glass Manufacturing Technician', 'glass-ceramics', 'Glass & Ceramics', 4.0, 'After attaining this qualification learner will be able to:
The course ''Advanced Certificate Course in Glass Manufacturing Practices'' has been introduced to generate skilled manpower to work in the field of glass manufacturing with latest technology as per the industrial requirement and expectations. 
• The aim of this Training Program is to prepare the trainees to meet the Industrial Expectation in the field of glass manufacturing. 
• Overall objective of this course to get the trainees acquainted with the modern glass manufacturing processes by providing hands-on training with the application of modern equipments& machines to enhance the practical skills.', 1200, 1200, '1001–1200', 'Version', '08 May 2025', '08 May 2028', 'MSME Technology Centre, Ministry of Micro Small And Medium Enterprises, New Delhi', 'MSME Technology Centre', 'Glass Plant Technician', 'Glass Plant
Supervisor', 'Cross Sectoral Qualification', 'N.A.', '{"Theory":"510","Practical":"330","EmployabilitySkills":"120","OJT_Mandatory":"240"}', false, '{}'::text[], '{"source_row": "1", "qualification_type": "Cross Sectoral Qualification", "version": "Version"}'::jsonb, 'Qualifications 02-10-2026 20_06_20.xlsx', true) ON CONFLICT (q_code, title) DO UPDATE SET sector_id = EXCLUDED.sector_id, nsqf_level = EXCLUDED.nsqf_level, description = EXCLUDED.description, min_notional_hours = EXCLUDED.min_notional_hours, max_notional_hours = EXCLUDED.max_notional_hours, notional_hours_range = EXCLUDED.notional_hours_range, is_pwd = EXCLUDED.is_pwd, pwd_categories = EXCLUDED.pwd_categories, updated_at = NOW();
