Demonstrate proficiency in teaching swimming techniques, including various strokes such as freestyle, breaststroke, backstroke, and butterfly.', 390, 690, '601–800', 'Version', '08 May 2025', '08 May 2028', 'Ganpat University', 'Ganpat University', 'Water Sports Assistant Trainer', 'Water Sports Trainer Level 4.0', 'General Qualification,Multi-Skill Qualification', 'N.A.', '{"Theory":"90","Practical":"210","EmployabilitySkills":"30","OJT_Mandatory":"60"}', false, '{}'::text[], '{"source_row": "39", "qualification_type": "General Qualification,Multi-Skill Qualification", "version": "Version"}'::jsonb, 'Qualifications 02-10-2026 20_14_41.xlsx', true) ON CONFLICT (q_code, title) DO UPDATE SET sector_id = EXCLUDED.sector_id, nsqf_level = EXCLUDED.nsqf_level, description = EXCLUDED.description, min_notional_hours = EXCLUDED.min_notional_hours, max_notional_hours = EXCLUDED.max_notional_hours, notional_hours_range = EXCLUDED.notional_hours_range, is_pwd = EXCLUDED.is_pwd, pwd_categories = EXCLUDED.pwd_categories, updated_at = NOW();
INSERT INTO nsqf_qualifications (q_code, title, sector_id, sector_name, nsqf_level, description, min_notional_hours, max_notional_hours, notional_hours_range, version, originally_approved, valid_till, awarding_body, certifying_bodies, proposed_occupation, progression_pathway, qualification_type, adopted_qualification, training_delivery_hours, is_pwd, pwd_categories, raw_metadata, source_file, is_active) VALUES ('QG-04-SP-04282-2025-V3-SPEFLSC', 'Swimming Pool Lifeguard', 'sports-physical-education-fitness-leisure', 'Sports, Physical Education, Fitness & Leisure', 4.0, 'The Swimming Pool Lifeguard will work at swimming pools to rescue swimmers from drowning and other pool related emergencies. The individual in this role would observe and supervise swimming areas to prevent accidents. The person is also responsible for making swimmers aware of dangerous situations.', 390, 390, '201–400', 'Version', '08 May 2025', '08 May 2028', 'Sports, Physical Education, Fitness and Leisure Skills Council (SPEFL)', 'SPEFL-SC', 'Swimming Pool Lifeguard', 'Level 5- Advance Lifeguard Open Water', 'General Qualification', 'N.A.', '{"Theory":"90","Practical":"180","EmployabilitySkills":"30","OJT_Mandatory":"90"}', false, '{}'::text[], '{"source_row": "40", "qualification_type": "General Qualification", "version": "Version"}'::jsonb, 'Qualifications 02-10-2026 20_14_41.xlsx', true) ON CONFLICT (q_code, title) DO UPDATE SET sector_id = EXCLUDED.sector_id, nsqf_level = EXCLUDED.nsqf_level, description = EXCLUDED.description, min_notional_hours = EXCLUDED.min_notional_hours, max_notional_hours = EXCLUDED.max_notional_hours, notional_hours_range = EXCLUDED.notional_hours_range, is_pwd = EXCLUDED.is_pwd, pwd_categories = EXCLUDED.pwd_categories, updated_at = NOW();
INSERT INTO nsqf_qualifications (q_code, title, sector_id, sector_name, nsqf_level, description, min_notional_hours, max_notional_hours, notional_hours_range, version, originally_approved, valid_till, awarding_body, certifying_bodies, proposed_occupation, progression_pathway, qualification_type, adopted_qualification, training_delivery_hours, is_pwd, pwd_categories, raw_metadata, source_file, is_active) VALUES ('QG-05-SP-00676-2025-V2-SPEFLSC', 'Swimming Instructor', 'sports-physical-education-fitness-leisure', 'Sports, Physical Education, Fitness & Leisure', 5.0, 'Swimming instructor, also known as a swimming teacher, helps children and adults develop proper swimming techniques. The individual plans and organizes swimming sessions and activities to improve the skill and fitness levels of participants. The individual ensures that safety standards are followed at all times and also deals with minor injuries of participants.', 660, 660, '601–800', 'Version', '08 May 2025', '08 May 2028', 'Sports, Physical Education, Fitness and Leisure Skills Council (SPEFL)', 'SPEFL-SC', 'Swimming Instructor', 'Level 6- Beach Captain', 'General Qualification', 'N.A.', '{"Theory":"150","Practical":"360","EmployabilitySkills":"60","OJT_Mandatory":"90"}', false, '{}'::text[], '{"source_row": "41", "qualification_type": "General Qualification", "version": "Version"}'::jsonb, 'Qualifications 02-10-2026 20_14_41.xlsx', true) ON CONFLICT (q_code, title) DO UPDATE SET sector_id = EXCLUDED.sector_id, nsqf_level = EXCLUDED.nsqf_level, description = EXCLUDED.description, min_notional_hours = EXCLUDED.min_notional_hours, max_notional_hours = EXCLUDED.max_notional_hours, notional_hours_range = EXCLUDED.notional_hours_range, is_pwd = EXCLUDED.is_pwd, pwd_categories = EXCLUDED.pwd_categories, updated_at = NOW();
INSERT INTO nsqf_qualifications (q_code, title, sector_id, sector_name, nsqf_level, description, min_notional_hours, max_notional_hours, notional_hours_range, version, originally_approved, valid_till, awarding_body, certifying_bodies, proposed_occupation, progression_pathway, qualification_type, adopted_qualification, training_delivery_hours, is_pwd, pwd_categories, raw_metadata, source_file, is_active) VALUES ('QG-04-TL-00461-2023-V1.1-TSSC', 'Technician – Automatic Train Protection System (ATPS)', 'telecom', 'Telecom', 4.0, 'A Technician – ATPS is responsible for performing various activities, such as the installation of Radio Frequency (RF) antennas, Ultra High Frequency (UHF) antennas, feeder cables, and Radio Frequency Identification Tags (RFID) tags. The individual is also responsible for laying, terminating, splicing, and rectifying fibre, optical fibre, and copper cables. The individual performs mast rigging operations, including mounting and aligning antennas', 450, 450, '401–600', 'Version', '26 May 2022', '26 May 2025', 'Telecom Sector Skill Council (TSSC)', 'Telecom Sector Skill Council', 'Project Engineering', 'Technician Supervisor – Automatic Train Protection System (ATPS)', 'Future Skills Qualification', 'N.A.', '{"Theory":"60","Practical":"150","EmployabilitySkills":"60","OJT_Mandatory":"180"}', false, '{}'::text[], '{"source_row": "1", "qualification_type": "Future Skills Qualification", "version": "Version"}'::jsonb, 'Qualifications 02-10-2026 20_14_49.xlsx', true) ON CONFLICT (q_code, title) DO UPDATE SET sector_id = EXCLUDED.sector_id, nsqf_level = EXCLUDED.nsqf_level, description = EXCLUDED.description, min_notional_hours = EXCLUDED.min_notional_hours, max_notional_hours = EXCLUDED.max_notional_hours, notional_hours_range = EXCLUDED.notional_hours_range, is_pwd = EXCLUDED.is_pwd, pwd_categories = EXCLUDED.pwd_categories, updated_at = NOW();
INSERT INTO nsqf_qualifications (q_code, title, sector_id, sector_name, nsqf_level, description, min_notional_hours, max_notional_hours, notional_hours_range, version, originally_approved, valid_till, awarding_body, certifying_bodies, proposed_occupation, progression_pathway, qualification_type, adopted_qualification, training_delivery_hours, is_pwd, pwd_categories, raw_metadata, source_file, is_active) VALUES ('QG-05-TL-00462-2023-V1.1-TSSC', 'Technical Supervisor – Automatic Train Protection System (ATPS)', 'telecom', 'Telecom', 5.0, 'A Technical Supervisor is responsible for carrying out various activities, such as planning and supervising the installation of stationary indigenous Automatic Train Protection System (iATP)-Kavach, Loco iATP-Kavach, and iATP-Kavach systems and sub-systems, e.g. RFID tags and readers. The individual is also responsible for soil testing and foundation of railway telecom towers, testing, and maintenance of iATP- Kavach systems and sub-systems, including fault localisation and troubleshooting. The individual is also responsible for OFC cable laying, jointing/splicing, termination, testing and documentation of the OFC cable plant. The person also supervises a team of technicians and workers.', 600, 600, '401–600', 'Version', '26 May 2022', '26 May 2025', 'Telecom Sector Skill Council (TSSC)', 'Telecom Sector Skill Council', 'Project Engineering', 'ATPS Head', 'Future Skills Qualification', 'N.A.', '{"Theory":"120","Practical":"210","EmployabilitySkills":"60","OJT_Mandatory":"210"}', false, '{}'::text[], '{"source_row": "2", "qualification_type": "Future Skills Qualification", "version": "Version"}'::jsonb, 'Qualifications 02-10-2026 20_14_49.xlsx', true) ON CONFLICT (q_code, title) DO UPDATE SET sector_id = EXCLUDED.sector_id, nsqf_level = EXCLUDED.nsqf_level, description = EXCLUDED.description, min_notional_hours = EXCLUDED.min_notional_hours, max_notional_hours = EXCLUDED.max_notional_hours, notional_hours_range = EXCLUDED.notional_hours_range, is_pwd = EXCLUDED.is_pwd, pwd_categories = EXCLUDED.pwd_categories, updated_at = NOW();
